+Keep Type arrows on grapheme boundaries in mixed-direction text
--- /dev/null
+++ publication-draft-01/body.md
@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@
+When text contains an RTL run, Type uses visual caret stops for Left/Right. A font can expose multiple shaping clusters inside one Unicode grapheme; in `हिन्दी שלום`, this can stop the caret at byte 12 instead of moving from byte 6 to byte 18. Filter visual stops by the text's grapheme boundaries before applying the existing directional ordering and distance logic.
+
+Add `caret_horizontal_cluster` for Type's two arrow callers while preserving the raw `caret_horizontal` API, same-x RTL ordering, soft-wrap tie exclusion, and line fallback. Separate raw shaping-cluster coverage from editing boundaries in the Hindi test, and add an actual Type-key regression with a plain-LTR control and an RTL suffix. The regression uses the existing installed-font order and explicit skip policy.
+
+Validation on pinned base `797e899c56957d292fe6140b4af18366d3cf0eb2`:
+
+- Original `cargo xtask ci`: all 10 stages passed. Workspace: 8,229 passed, 0 failed, 12 ignored across 143 summaries; separate no-bundled-fonts check: 1 passed; 23 Wasm packages checked.
+- Captured CI success does not establish that every font-dependent assertion ran: allowed font/capability returns can report success.
+- A separate private 73f causal pair reached the mixed-direction Right failure (12 instead of 18) before the correction and passed both original cases afterward. That proof is limited to its recorded font/input prerequisites and is not transferred to this 797 publication fixture.
+- [ ] Complete and inspect the original one-scene 1280×960 production-app egui_kittest/wgpu render. Its recipe is ready but unrun. Metadata/bootstrap and resolved dependency-edge qualification establish readiness only, not UI evidence.
